# Cell from playpick: mode=clear, spec=paladin:retribution, style=wander,
# size=25, difficulty=heroic, view=844x390,touch, save=fresh. 25-heroic is
# locked at the door on a fresh save (src/progress.ts's RUNGS chain: a fresh
# save's `unlocked` is 0, and 25-heroic on the first boss sits at chain index
# 3) -- substituted the setup screen's own default, 10-player normal, same
# substitution the two prior attempts at this cell made.
#
# Third attempt at this exact cell. The previous two (plans -1, -2, see
# commits 2641416 and e4be536) both started `evening wander 200 14` in the
# background and ended their own turn saying they would read the result
# later -- the exact mistake docs/playtest.md names by name ("There is no
# later"), and a `claude -p` session has no later: both left a plan file and
# no ledger line.
#
# This is the same walk, run to completion inside this session rather than
# handed to a background notification that a one-shot session can never
# receive. A single evening is longer than one tool call's own timeout can
# safely cover, so it is split into two chunks against a shared --profile and
# --out: the first chunk walks in and plays three rooms, the second reloads
# the page (the `open` below) and resumes with `tap raid` -- proving the
# save-and-resume feature the README describes ("RAID resumes standing where
# you stood") rather than working around the split in secret -- then plays
# three more. The journal is one continuous file across both.
open
targets
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:paladin:retribution
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot arrive-threshold
state
targets
evening wander 130 3
shot after-evening-a
state
says
open
tap raid
waitscreen fight 15
shot resumed
state
evening wander 130 3
shot after-evening-b
state
says
targets
ui
bill
